    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0617" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg497"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 213.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge with thanks
                    the receipt of your letter No. 340, of the 25th October, regarding the
                    Newfoundland fishery question, and to assure you that I highly appreciate the
                    spirit in which it was written.</p>
                <p>It will be in no way disagreeable to me that you should take the course you
                    propose with regard to my letter of the 20th October, and I will with your
                    permission communicate to the Newfoundland government, for the information of
                    their people on the treaty coast, the substance of your reply.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. M. Durand.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
